{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Please no, Adonai.</b> This is secular (profane speech), and therefore it completed the verse here, and afterwards returned to pray to HaShem: 'Please now, your servant has found favor.' And according to the masoretic tradition it is holy. And it is written with alef-dalet."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The comment addresses whether the divine name here is read as secular or holy; 'it is written with alef-dalet' refers to the consonantal spelling אדני."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:54.220314784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}